-- title:
--   Energy of the separately contracted, vertex-deleted Ising interaction
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite graph on the vertex set $V=\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ with separately indexed edges $e$ (parallel edges allowed), endpoints $\ell(e)\neq r(e)$ and couplings $K_e\ge0$, and let $I,J,F\subseteq V$ be arbitrary vertex sets. On the set $V\setminus F$ of free vertices let $\approx$ be the equivalence relation generated by $x\approx y$ whenever $x,y\in I$ or $x,y\in J$; write $[x]$ for the class of $x$ and $Q=(V\setminus F)/{\approx}$ for the set of classes. Thus the free parts of $I$ and of $J$ are each collapsed (into a single class if they meet), and every other free vertex is a class of its own. Let $E_F=\{e:\ \ell(e)\notin F,\ r(e)\notin F\}$ be the set of edges that survive deletion of $F$.
--
--   The *contracted interaction* has vertex set $Q$ and bond set $E_F$, the bond $e$ joining $[\ell(e)]$ to $[r(e)]$ with coupling $K_e$; self-loops created by the contraction and parallel bonds are kept. For a field $g$ on the free vertices, the contracted field sums $g$ over each class, $\bar g_q=\sum_{v\in V\setminus F,\ [v]=q}g_v$, and the energy of a configuration $c\in\{-1,+1\}^Q$ is $\widehat{\mathcal H}_{\bar g}(c)=\sum_{e\in E_F}K_e\,c_{[\ell(e)]}c_{[r(e)]}+\sum_{q\in Q}\bar g_q\,c_q$.
--
--   **Theorem.** For every field $g:V\setminus F\to\mathbb{R}$ and every $c\in\{-1,+1\}^Q$,
--   $$
--   \widehat{\mathcal H}_{\bar g}(c)=\mathcal H^{\mathrm{del}}_F\big(c\circ[\cdot]\big)+\sum_{v\in V\setminus F}g_v\,c_{[v]},
--   $$
--   where $c\circ[\cdot]$ is the configuration $v\mapsto c_{[v]}$ of the free vertices and $\mathcal H^{\mathrm{del}}_F(\sigma)=\sum_{e\in E_F}K_e\sigma_{\ell(e)}\sigma_{r(e)}$ is the zero-field energy of the vertex-deleted graph.
--
--   The contracted model, with the fields summed over each class, therefore has exactly the energy of the vertex-deleted model with field $g$, evaluated on block-constant configurations. Combined with the exact elimination of pinned spins (where $g$ is the field induced by the pins), this identifies the pinned Ising marginal of two terminal blocks with a genuine Ising model on a contracted graph.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $Q$ is `ContractedVertex G I J F`, the quotient by `comparisonSetoid G I J F ∅`; the contracted interaction is `contractedInteraction G I J F`, a `PairInteraction` (self-loops allowed) whose bonds form the subtype `KeptEdge G F`; $\bar g$ is `quotientField (comparisonSetoid G I J F ∅) g`; and the energy is `interactionEnergy`. No disjointness of $I$, $J$, $F$ is assumed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Probability/Ising/Contraction.lean#L193-L210

